Fri Oct 23 07:12:14 UTC 2026 - Paolo Stivanin <info@paolostivanin.com>

- Update to 0.10.0 (upstream tag v0.10.0, 2026-10-22):
  * 0.9.0: PNG export with a transparent background; PDF export
    stores each shared slide backdrop once; a .ppsx opened last
    starts its slide show; Align to Slide/Selected Objects
  * 0.9.0: AutoFormat superscripts ordinals; change case across
    formatting runs; flipping a rotated shape mirrors the
    rotation; Edit Points freeform conversion is one undo step
  * 0.9.0: imported chart parts survive native saves; unreadable
    PPTX slides are reported instead of silently dropped
  * 0.9.0 hardening (no CVE assigned): absurd effect sizes from
    a file are capped (a huge glow asked for 34 GB), duplicate
    shape ids get fresh ones, shape geometry and comment.delete
    indices are bounds-checked
  * 0.10.0: thumbnails render only the slides in view; an empty
    text line takes the size of its end mark; invalid slide
    indices are rejected; OPC targets strip the URI fragment
    before percent-decoding; animation triggers on deleted
    shapes are cleared
  * 0.10.0: macOS Finder/Dock open support (fmv-macos-events,
    macOS-only, not built here); docs/CI only otherwise
  * Re-vendor (update=true): only point bumps (icu 2.4, cc,
    memmap2, zerovec, yoke, tinystr, webbrowser, crc32fast) under
    already-listed licences; licence set and Legal-Review-Notice
    unchanged; cargo_vendor reports all lockfiles audited, no
    RUSTSEC advisories.
- Set the fixed metainfo release date to 2026-10-22 (v0.10.0).

